    "remaining_risks": [
      "The native embedded-audit lane cannot represent the auditor that actually ran. auditor_tool and auditor_model carry the schema's fallback values; they are not a claim that no audit occurred. The audit ran, returned PASS with zero blockers and zero must-fix, and its verbatim report is at proof/TP-DMX-SECOND-BRAIN-ADR-CONTRACT-EVIDENCE-001/AUDITOR_REPAIR_2_REPORT.md.",
      "Because of that representation gap, validate_change_contract.py and pre-commit still fail. A PASS from the independent audit does not turn them green: they fail for a schema-representation cause, not for anything about the contract evidence. Repairing that schema is out of lane per packet section 1.",
      "Residual, confirmed by the producer and documented in the validator header before the audit ran: with FROZEN_INVENTORY_SHA256 and the supersession receipt both rewritten, clause booleans that no Group S pin covers can be flipped while the validator exits 0. A consistent bilateral edit with the pin left alone fails at A09, which is the false-green round 1 found. A checker cannot defend its own constants.",
      "The census worksheet labels 25 clauses UNCHANGED that the computed supersession record lists as modified. All 25 are rule_type renames under the new taxonomy with byte-identical machine values. The receipt is authoritative; see AUDIT_R2_RESIDUALS.json.",
      "The operator ruling is bound to this freeze by presence and by naming the superseded inventory hash, not by a content hash linking the ruling to the new inventory bytes. The ruling predates those bytes, so that binding cannot exist."
    ],
